**Job Summary**

The Nutrition Services department is dedicated to providing excellent nutritional care, quality meals to our patients and creating an exceptional learning environment for our students. We contribute to the Hospital community in the following ways:

Education; Learning opportunities for dietetic students through our dietetic internship program;

Research; – Research to improve our knowledge of nutrition with the goal of enhancing the care we provide our patients;

Patient Food Services; Healthy meals for inpatients;

Retail Food Services; High quality meals for family members, staff and outpatients;

Resources; Useful links to on-line information about health and nutrition.

The primary responsibility of the Operations Leader – Nutrition Services is to overlook the Nutrition Services operations to ensure a safe delivery of well-balanced, clean, attractive and nutritious meals to all designated patients. A high standard of quality and accuracy must be obtained for patient tray preparation, assembly, delivery and collection. They must ensure a high level of sanitation and hygiene for patient cafeteria services and use resources efficiently to contribute to financial goals.

**Main Responsibilities:**

Monitor and record fridge temperatures;

Work with teams to ensure accuracy of menus and diets on patient trays, nourishments and supplements;

Monitor quality and food temperatures during food holding and handling procedures;

Ensure that all food handling procedures meet the standards of City of Toronto Public Health inspectors;

Ensure all chemicals are handled properly and labeled following WHIMIS legislation and standards;

Conduct hand hygiene audits for Nutrition staff;

In liaison with the Dietitians and Food Services Manager, ensures that the therapeutic menu requirements are maintained.

Responsible for the maintenance and service of all equipment; should be functional, safe and clean;

Ensures adherence to quality assurance, risk management, occupational health and safety act and sanitation code.

Oversee the daily operations of the Food Service Department in order to ensure efficient and correct workflow;

Keep track of inventory on some items and ordering food and other supplies;

Work closely with nutritionists and dietitians to plan and prepare both the regular and special diet menus in the hospital;

Complete daily sanitation audits, ordering, waste management audits;

Conduct patient satisfaction surveys; and conduct rounds on inpatient units during meal service;

Informs Food Services Manager & Lead Chef of meal service, menu items and production requirements/concerns;

Plans and chairs monthly staff meetings, as delegated;

Manage budgetary resources (e.g. food supplies and labor) in a cost effective manner;

Complete Safety First and WSIB forms as needed, and follow up with Employee Health Department, as required.

Responsible for training, orientation, employee evaluations, and scheduling;

Responsible for disciplining, staff payroll, investigating, reporting and recording of injuries or incidents;

Ensures personal protective equipment is worn by staff at all times, as required;

Manage the performance of general staff;

Replace staff for sick leave; vacations; absences;

Document incidents in employee files; follow up with Manager if disciplinary action is required.

Attend Disciplinary meetings/Fact findings and closure meetings with Human Resources as required

Ordering supplies and maintaining inventory;

Scheduling.

**Qualifications:**

2-5 years’ experience in food services;

Knowledge of Occupational Health & Safety Act;

Sound knowledge of institutional food service supervision, sanitation and safety;

Therapeutic, nutrition and dietetic knowledge required

Must hold a current Food Handler’s Certificate

Must have completed a 2 year Nutrition Management program or 4 year Dietitian program

Must have current membership in Canadian Society of Nutrition Management

**Must be available to work 3 out of 4 weekends but will mostly be scheduled for every other weekend. As well the shift times are 12:15 - 8:15 pm / 1:00 - 8:15 pm and 6 am to 2 pm**




Unity Health Toronto is committed to creating an accessible and inclusive organization. We strive to provide a recruitment process that is barrier-free and in compliance with the Accessibility for Ontarians with Disabilities Act (AODA) and the Ontario Human Rights Code. We understand that you may require an accommodation at any stage of the recruitment process. When you are contacted, please inform the Talent Acquisition Specialist and we will work with you to meet your accommodation needs. We want to emphasize that all accommodation requests are handled with the utmost confidentiality, respecting your privacy and dignity.


#LI-MR1

**Position Summary**
--------------------

**Join a company where the work you do makes a difference!** We are **One Team** with **One Goal**. At STERIS Applied Sterilization Technologies (AST), it’s our philosophy and our way of doing business. Through a network of over 50 facilities globally, STERIS AST has been committed to providing contract sterilization services to the medical device, pharmaceutical, consumer, and industrial communities for over 40 years. Our irradiation and gas sterilization services ensure the safety of those who use these products, including our families, our friends, and ourselves.

We are seeking an experienced **Quality Assurance Manager**, to lead the Quality function at our **Whitby, ON**, facility. You will play a key role in shaping quality strategy, driving continuous improvement, ensuring regulatory compliance, and building a culture of operational excellence.

As the QA Manager, you will provide strategic leadership for the site's **Quality Management System (QMS)**, ensuring compliance with global regulatory and quality standards while driving a culture of continuous improvement. You will oversee quality systems, regulatory compliance, supplier quality, process quality, and quality improvement initiatives across the Whitby facility. You will partner closely with site leadership to strengthen operational performance, maintain audit readiness, and ensure compliance with standards including ISO 9001, ISO 13485, MDSAP, FDA 21 CFR Part 820/211, and EU MDR.As the site's **Management Representative**, you will champion quality excellence, lead quality strategy, and help ensure STERIS continues to deliver safe, reliable, and compliant services to customers around the world.

Please note that this is an on-site leadership position based in our facility in Whitby, ON, with up to 20% travel.

**What You'll do as a Quality Assurance Manager - QMS & Compliance**
--------------------------------------------------------------------

**Provide Strategic Quality Leadership**

* Lead the site's Quality organization and establish a culture focused on quality, compliance, accountability, and continuous improvement;
* Partner with the Site Leadership Team to align quality objectives with business goals and operational priorities;
* Serve as the site's Management Representative and lead Management Review activities.

**Drive Compliance & Regulatory Excellence**

* Ensure continued compliance with applicable standards and regulations, including: ISO 9001, ISO 13485, MDSAP, FDA 21 CFR Part 820 and Part 211, EU MDR;
* Maintain inspection and audit readiness while supporting successful customer, regulatory, and certification audits;
* Act as the site's Person Responsible for Regulatory Compliance (PRRC) in accordance with EU MDR requirements.

**Advance Continuous Improvement**

* Lead site-wide quality improvement initiatives using data-driven decision making;
* Monitor key performance indicators and implement corrective and preventive actions that improve quality, efficiency, and customer satisfaction;
* Collaborate with Operations and Engineering teams to strengthen process capability and process controls.

**Support Product & Supplier Quality**

* Provide quality leadership throughout product and process development activities;
* Oversee supplier quality programs and risk-based supplier qualification processes;
* Ensure effective complaint investigation and resolution processes that drive meaningful improvements.

**Develop High-Performing Teams**

* Coach, mentor, and develop Quality team members;
* Foster collaboration across Manufacturing, Engineering, Regulatory Affairs, Supply Chain, and Operations functions;
* Build organizational capability through leadership, talent development, and succession planning.

**The Experience, Skills and Abilities Needed**
-----------------------------------------------

*Required*

* Bachelor's degree in Engineering or another relevant technical discipline;
* 8+ years of experience in Quality Systems, Quality Engineering, Manufacturing Quality, or related disciplines within a regulated industry;
* 8+ years of experience working within ISO-certified environments;
* 2+ years of experience leading and developing teams;
* Strong working knowledge of quality systems, risk management, auditing, and regulatory compliance;
* Eligibility to meet EU MDR Article 15 requirements for PRRC responsibilities;
* Demonstrated ability to influence cross-functional stakeholders and drive organizational change;
* Excellent communication, problem-solving, and decision-making skills.

*Preferred*

* Experience in medical devices, healthcare, pharmaceuticals, sterilization, or other highly regulated industries;
* Knowledge of Quality System Regulations (QSR), GMP requirements, and international quality standards;
* Experience with statistical analysis tools, process improvement methodologies and Lean manufacturing environments;
* ASQ certifications are considered an asset.

**What STERIS Offers**
----------------------

This is an opportunity to join a company that will invest in you for the long-term. STERIS wouldn’t be where it is today without our incredible people, who take true pride in their work. That’s why we share in our success together by rewarding employees for their hard work.

*Here is just a brief overview of what we offer:*

* Market Competitive Pay;
* A range of employee benefits, including:
  + A comprehensive and flexible group insurance plan – offering various options and approximately 90% covered by STERIS. This plan includes prescription drug coverage, vision care, paramedical services, and dental care;
  + Telemedicine services;
  + An Employee Assistance Program (EAP);
  + A bank of personal days (5 days);
  + Paid-time off;
  + A day off on your work anniversary;
  + A group RRSP with employer contributions from STERIS, up to 3% of annual salary;
  + A corporate bonus program;
* An experienced and multidisciplinary team;
* A safe environment at the forefront of continuous improvement.
* Excellent opportunities for advancement and stable long-term career.

#LI-AK

This posting is for an existing vacancy within our organization.

Pay range for this opportunity is $95,000 - $110,000 CAD/year. This position is incentive plan eligible, at target earnings of 10%, depending on performance.

STERIS strives to be an Equal Opportunity Employer. STERIS is committed to treating all people in a way that allows them to ‎maintain their dignity and independence. We believe in integration and equal ‎opportunity. Accommodations are available throughout the recruitment process ‎and applicants with a disability may request to be accommodated throughout the ‎recruitment process.‎ We will work with all applicants to accommodate their individual accessibility ‎needs.

**SUMMARY:** Reporting to the President, the National Director of Operations is responsible for the operational and administrative performance of the entire Scandinave Group. As a member of the leadership team, this person defines and rolls out the Group’s operational vision, ensures the excellence and consistency of the customer experience, and oversees the general managers of each site. They ensure the achievement of the quality, profitability and sustainability objectives that support the Group’s growth, while optimizing and standardizing business practices.

TASKS AND RESPONSIBILITIES

Strategy and governance


* Develop, with the President and the leadership team, the Scandinave Group’s operational strategy and ensure its rollout across all spas;
* Represent operations before the leadership committee and report regularly to the President on the Group’s performance and issues;

Team and manager development


* Lead, mobilize and evaluate the general managers and their teams across the various departments, including massage therapy, customer service, reservations, housekeeping, maintenance and the thermal experience;
* Foster the training, development and succession of managers and ensure the effectiveness of team communication and training tools;

Finance and purchasing


* Participate in the preparation and monitoring of operating and capital budgets; analyze financial and operational results and implement the corrective measures required to meet profitability targets;
* Define the Group’s centralized purchasing strategy, oversee the entire process from obtaining quotes to product delivery, and manage relationships with key suppliers;

Operational standards and continuous improvement


* Establish, in collaboration with the President and the spa managers, the Group’s operational and quality standards and ensure their uniform application so that the entire Group progresses in a coordinated way;
* Oversee the standardization and optimization of administrative and operational procedures and processes across all departments;
* Establish and ensure the ongoing updating of operational procedures and standards;
* Ensure that teams are trained in the operational standards;
* Define and track the Group’s key performance indicators (KPIs) using dashboards and identify, with the managers, solutions to achieve objectives;
* Implement an audit program to validate compliance with operational and regulatory standards and ensure the necessary corrective actions are carried out;

Site maintenance and renovation


* Oversee site maintenance and renovation projects, in collaboration with the maintenance directors and general managers, to ensure facilities are in good condition and work proceeds smoothly;
* Ensure adherence to the priorities of the maintenance program and the preventive maintenance plan;
* Support the development and integration of new sites, in collaboration with the President.

EXPERIENCE


* At least 10 years of experience in operations management, including a minimum of 5 years in a leadership position;
* Multi-site management experience (a significant asset);
* Proven experience in monitoring financial performance, key performance indicators (KPIs) and managing teams of managers;
* Experience developing and implementing standards, procedures and continuous improvement processes;
* Knowledge of the spa, hospitality or tourism industry (a significant asset);
* Experience and interest in maintenance, construction and renovation (a significant asset).

REQUIREMENTS, SKILLS AND PERSONAL QUALITIES

Requirements


* Bachelor’s degree in business administration, operations management or a related field (an asset);
* Bilingualism required, in French and English, both oral and written;
* Knowledge of the Zenoti point-of-sale system (an asset);
* Knowledge of artificial intelligence tools and a strong interest in their use and deployment
* Availability for frequent travel to each of the Group’s current sites (Whistler, Blue Mountain, Mont-Tremblant and Edmonton (upcoming)), approximately one (1) week per month (about 25%);
* During initial training, travel will be more frequent.

Skills and personal qualities


* Unifying leadership and strategic vision, with the ability to mobilize teams spread across several sites;
* Proactive and enjoys working in a constantly evolving environment;
* Attentive to needs and differing points of view;
* Ability to make decisions that are not unanimous and to explain the chosen direction in order to maintain engagement (an iron fist in a velvet glove);
* Excellent business acumen, analytical rigour and the ability to drive performance using indicators;
* Ability to work “hands-on” while assuming a strategic role.

CONDITIONS

Benefits


* Hybrid work (3 days in the office and 2 days remote);
* Work in a wellness setting, in an enchanting environment across Canada;
* Collaborate with a strong and dynamic leadership team;
* Access to the thermal circuit and massage experience;
* Group insurance with paid employer participation (60%).

**Sommaire du poste**
Relevant du Directeur, Infrastructure TI, le Gestionnaire technique réseau est responsable du leadership opérationnel, de l’exploitation, de la maintenance et de l’amélioration continue de l’infrastructure réseau d’entreprise de l’organisation. Il supervise les opérations réseau dans les bureaux corporatifs, les centres de distribution, les centres de données, les environnements infonuagiques et les magasins, tout en dirigeant une équipe de huit professionnels des réseaux responsables de la disponibilité, de la performance, de la sécurité et de l’évolutivité des services réseau. Le poste est basé au siège social de Dollarama à Montréal (horaire de travail hybride) et assure la supervision des équipes réseau au Canada et en Australie.


**Responsabilités**
**Opérations réseau et disponibilité des services**

* Diriger l’équipe des opérations réseau du Canada et de l’Australie;
* Participer occasionnellement à des réunions en soirée avec l’Australie et les employés relevant à distance de l’équipe de Melbourne;
* Assurer la disponibilité, la fiabilité, la performance et la capacité des services réseau LAN, WAN, Wi-Fi, SD-WAN, Internet, infonuagiques et des centres de données;
* Superviser la surveillance du réseau, la gestion des alertes, la réponse aux incidents, la gestion des problèmes, l’analyse des causes profondes et les processus d’escalade opérationnelle;
* Coordonner la gestion des interruptions majeures et soutenir le rétablissement des services réseau.

**Déploiement des réseaux en magasin**

* Superviser les déploiements et les migrations réseau pour les nouveaux magasins et les magasins existants;
* Définir et maintenir les processus de préparation, de provisionnement automatisé, de validation et de vérification de l’état des réseaux;
* Coordonner les prérequis réseau, l’attribution des équipements, la connectivité et la préparation opérationnelle nécessaires aux ouvertures et conversions de magasins;
* Mettre en place des méthodes de déploiement reproductibles afin de réduire les configurations manuelles et les dépendances opérationnelles.

**Architecture réseau, normes et amélioration continue**

* Définir et maintenir les normes réseau, les conventions de nommage, les procédures opérationnelles, la documentation technique et les pratiques de soutien;
* Améliorer les processus de déploiement et d’exploitation réseau grâce à l’automatisation, la standardisation et des contrôles mesurables;
* Collaborer avec les équipes Infrastructure, Cybersécurité, Infonuagique, Applications et Gestion de projets afin de concevoir des solutions sécuritaires et résilientes;
* Contribuer aux feuilles de route réseau, à la planification de la capacité, au renouvellement technologique et aux initiatives de modernisation.

**Gestion des actifs, des licences et du cycle de vie**

* Superviser l’inventaire des équipements réseau, les licences et la couverture de soutien;
* Coordonner l’intégration, le transfert, le renouvellement, le remplacement et le retrait des équipements réseau pour les bureaux corporatifs et les entrepôts.

**Gestion des fournisseurs, des prestataires et des finances**

* Gérer les relations avec les fournisseurs de télécommunications, les fournisseurs de technologies réseau, les entrepreneurs et les fournisseurs de services gérés;
* Coordonner les escalades techniques, les interventions de soutien, les mises à niveau, les services professionnels et les activités d’implantation;
* Soutenir les activités d’approvisionnement, la planification budgétaire, les prévisions financières, les renouvellements de contrats et l’optimisation des coûts liés aux services et technologies réseau.

**Leadership d’équipe et gouvernance**

* Fournir du leadership, de l’accompagnement technique, du coaching, de la priorisation des charges de travail et du soutien lors des escalades aux membres de l’équipe réseau au Canada et en Australie;
* Établir les attentes en matière de service, les indicateurs opérationnels, les contrôles et les objectifs d’amélioration continue;
* Favoriser le transfert des connaissances, une documentation efficace, une gestion rigoureuse des changements et la collaboration entre les équipes.

**Exigences du poste**

* Baccalauréat en technologie de l’information, en informatique, en génie ou dans un domaine connexe, ou expérience professionnelle équivalente;
