At Cameco we understand the value of a diverse workforce and we embrace, encourage and support workplace inclusion and diversity. New ideas, perspectives, experiences, and expertise make Cameco stronger. We are committed to building a diverse workforce reflective of the communities we operate in. Our vision is to create a culture where inclusion is the goal, and a diverse and representative workforce is our measure of success. Cameco is committed to providing an inclusive selection process, free from systemic barriers. support employment equity and encourage all members of underrepresented groups (i.e., women, Indigenous peoples, persons with disabilities and members of racialized groups/visible minorities) to voluntarily disclose. Cameco welcomes applicants from all backgrounds, abilities, and experiences to apply.



**About Us**

Cameco is one of the largest global providers of the uranium fuel needed to power a secure energy future. Utilities around the world rely on our nuclear fuel products to generate safe, reliable, emissions-free nuclear power. Cameco’s corporate office is based in Saskatoon. We have mining operations and projects in northern Saskatchewan, Kazakhstan, the United States and Australia. We are also a leading supplier of uranium refining, conversion, and fuel manufacturing services from our operations in Ontario.



**The Role**

The Manager, AI leads Cameco's AI tooling, platform and delivery processes, as well as the AI Development team. Reporting to the Director, AI, People Change & Automation, this role owns the AI platform capability, developer tooling and model lifecycle, plans and prioritizes AI delivery, and partners with architects, business teams and vendors to deliver secure, responsible AI solutions that create business value.



**In this role, you will:**

* Lead, coach and develop the AI Development team, managing performance and building team capability.
* Own Cameco's AI tooling and processes, developer tooling and internal developer portal, model lifecycle and AI delivery practices.
* Define and continuously improve AI delivery processes, golden-path workflows, coding standards and reusable patterns in partnership with senior technical staff.
* Plan, prioritize and manage the AI delivery pipeline, translating business use cases into scoped, deliverable solutions.
* Ensure AI solutions apply Cameco's AI governance framework, including security, privacy and responsible AI controls.
* Partner with architects, platform teams and vendors to align tooling, roadmap and delivery.
* Report delivery progress, platform and tooling health, risks and value realized to the Director, and support budget and resource planning.


**Required:**

* bachelor's degree or diploma in computer science, software engineering, data science, or related field;
* minimum ten years of software/AI development experience, including delivery of AI/ML solutions and hands-on AI tooling or platform work;
* equivalent combination of education and work experience considered;
* experience leading or supervising a development team, or acting as a technical or delivery lead;
* experience with AI/ML platforms and containerized or cloud-native environments; and
* demonstrated experience with agile planning, prioritization, coaching and performance management.


**Recommended:**

* experience with Red Hat OpenShift, OpenShift AI, Kubernetes, internal developer portals and CI/CD practices;
* experience delivering AI solutions involving model integration, fine-tuning, retrieval-augmented generation (RAG) and agentic frameworks;
* experience with enterprise data integration across cloud and on-premise sources (GCP/BigQuery, Microsoft 365, file shares) and API-based design;
* knowledge of AI governance and security practices, including NIST AI RMF, identity and access management and responsible AI;
* experience managing vendor relationships and technology roadmaps;
* experience delivering solutions in regulated or security-sensitive industries; and
* strong communication skills with the ability to engage both technical and business audiences.


**Conditions of Employment:**

* background check.


